      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I have a clear picture. The original test has several understandability issues:\n- Many unused imports (17 of them)\n- A vague variable name `test12`\n- No comments explaining integer division truncation behavior or why `dividedBy(5)` and `dividedBy(6)` both yield 2\n\nLet me write the improved test.Now I'll compile-check it.The improved test compiles successfully. The refactored version removes 17 unused imports, renames `test12` to the descriptive `twelveMonths`, and adds concise comments explaining integer truncation and the negative-divisor behavior — all without changing any method calls or expected values."
